---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const email = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL || 'bryce@originslynk.com';
---

<Base
  title="Website terms"
  description="Terms for using the OriginsLynk website and submitting a service inquiry."
>
  <section class="section-cream page-hero">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website terms</p>
      <h1>Plain boundaries for using this website.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These terms apply to originslynk.com and its service-request form. They do not replace
        a written proposal or service agreement for paid work.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted updated">Effective August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container container-narrow legal-copy">
      <article>
        <h2>Who operates this site</h2>
        <p>OriginsLynk is operated by Primitive Origins LLC in Anderson, South Carolina.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Website information is not a service agreement</h2>
        <p>
          This site describes general services, starting prices, common boundaries, and
          examples. An engagement begins only after the client and OriginsLynk agree to a
          written scope and price and complete any stated acceptance and payment requirements.
          The signed engagement documents control if they differ from general website copy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may use this site to learn about OriginsLynk and submit a genuine business inquiry. Do not:</p>
        <ul class="crosslist">
          <li>Interfere with the site, evade security controls, or probe it without written authorization</li>
          <li>Use the form for spam, impersonation, harassment, unlawful activity, or malicious content</li>
          <li>Submit passwords, private keys, payment-card details, health information, or confidential client records</li>
          <li>Misrepresent website content or OriginsLynk services as your own</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>AI, automation, and professional judgment</h2>
        <p>
          AI-generated and automated outputs can be incomplete, inaccurate, delayed, or
          unsuitable for a particular use. OriginsLynk provides workflow design and technical
          implementation—not legal, tax, accounting, medical, financial, employment, or
          regulatory advice. See the <a href="/ai-automation-notice">AI &amp; Automation Notice</a>
          for the operating boundaries used across services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Third-party services and availability</h2>
        <p>
          The website and client solutions may depend on hosting, email, internet access,
          business accounts, AI services, integrations, and other third-party providers.
          Providers may change or interrupt features outside OriginsLynk’s control. Required
          subscriptions and usage charges are disclosed during proposal and onboarding and
          remain the client’s responsibility unless the written proposal says otherwise.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Ownership of site content</h2>
        <p>
          Primitive Origins LLC owns the original text, design, graphics, and branding on this
          site except for identified third-party material. You may view and share links to the
          site when evaluating the services. Copying, republishing, selling, or presenting the
          site content or branding as your own requires written permission.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>
          Website content and these terms may be updated as the services and operating
          practices change. The effective date above identifies the current version. Questions
          may be sent to <a href={`mailto:${email}?subject=Website%20terms%20question`}>{email}</a>.
          Information submitted through the site is handled according to the
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero h1 { max-width: 18ch; }
  .page-hero .lede { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .updated { margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .legal-copy { display: grid; gap: var(--space-7); }
  .legal-copy article { padding-top: var(--space-5); border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .legal-copy h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  .legal-copy p, .legal-copy ul { margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
